/*
 * Declares the SliceType class.
 *
 * A SliceType represents a view over a contiguous sequence of elements of a
 * single inner type. Unlike arrays, slices do not have a compile‑time size:
 * their length is stored in the slice value itself and is known only at
 * runtime. Slices are lightweight, borrowing containers that reference memory
 * owned elsewhere.
 *
 * Slices:
 *   - wrap a single inner type T,
 *   - may optionally carry a compile‑time‑known size when available,
 *   - cannot contain movable types,
 *   - always borrow data,
 *   - derive mutability from the slice itself and from the inner type.
 *
 * <hr>
 *
 * @Package: ymirc
